    "step8_outcome_verification": {
      "primary_intent": "The user wanted the agent to open Project Gutenberg eBook #1342 (Pride and Prejudice) and accurately transcribe four on-page metadata fields (author, Release Date, Last Update, language) plus confirm whether three specific download format labels (EPUB3, Plain Text (accessible), Download HTML (zip)) are available\u2014without downloading anything. A reasonable user would not be flexible on the correctness of the Release Date/Last Update values (must be the Gutenberg-labeled fields) or on making up availability that isn\u2019t supported.",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: The agent\u2019s inclusion of extra descriptive text with EPUB3 (\u201c\u2605 Recommended for most devices\u201d) is minor and doesn\u2019t change the availability answer. Also, reporting format availability as \u201cnot visible in current viewport\u201d rather than definitively \u201cnot available\u201d is acceptable and cautious.\n\nCritical issues: The agent reported specific values for Release Date (\u201cJun 1, 1998\u201d) and Last Update (\u201cSep 1, 2026\u201d) that are not shown in the provided screenshots, and the task explicitly required using the Gutenberg page\u2019s \u201cRelease Date\u201d and \u201cLast Update\u201d labels and preserving displayed dates exactly. Given the evidence, these two fields appear unsupported and likely fabricated, which is a major correctness failure because those dates are part of the primary deliverable.\n\nWhat was done correctly: Screenshots show the Pride and Prejudice Gutenberg page and an \u201cAbout this eBook\u201d table with Author \u201cAusten, Jane, 1775-1817\u201d and Language \u201cEnglish,\u201d matching the agent\u2019s output. Screenshot 1 visually confirms the EPUB3 label is present in the download section, so marking EPUB3 as available is supported. For Plain Text (accessible) and Download HTML (zip), the screenshots do not show those labels; the agent did not falsely claim they are available, instead stating they are not visible in the current viewport evidence, which aligns with what\u2019s shown.\n\nOverall outcome: Because two of the four required metadata fields (Release Date and Last Update) are provided as exact dates without evidentiary support and contrary to the constraint to use the on-page labeled fields, the user would not receive a trustworthy, task-complete record. This is a critical failure despite the correct author/language and partial format checking.",
      "output_success": false
    },
